From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sdk_dpaa: enable Rx checksum validation and GRO safely

dpa_fix_features() cleared NETIF_F_RXCSUM unconditionally ("not
supported through ethtool yet"), so every frame the stack receives
from a DPAA port was checksummed in software and none took GRO. On a
WireGuard tunnel's receive CPU the outer UDP checksum alone was 7% of
its time. The support exists: dpa_set_features() switches the parser's
L4 check and _dpa_process_parse_results() trusts it only when the parse
result says the checksum passed. Stop masking the feature.

That exposes GRO, which had never run. With CONFIG_FSL_ASK_QMAN_PORTAL_NAPI
a portal is drained by the portal's NAPI, or by VWD's, never by a port's,
so _dpa_rx() GROs into a NAPI that is not polling. The SDK's poll context
(qman_portal_napi_gro_receive()) records such a NAPI and flushes it when
the DQRR poll ends, so nothing waits in a GRO list nobody flushes.

GRO also stamps each skb with the receiving NAPI's id, and a socket that
has received one may busy-poll that NAPI (SO_BUSY_POLL needs no
privilege): napi_busy_loop() runs its poll from the socket's task, on
any CPU, with the portal's dequeue interrupt still enabled, and
qman_p_poll_dqrr() BUG()s -- a panic any local user could cause. A
portal is one CPU's, drained only by the poll its interrupt scheduled,
so every NAPI that drains one -- the portal's own and each port's, and
VWD's in cdx -- is registered NO_BUSY_POLL, as netif_napi_add_tx()
does: none is in the NAPI hash, so none has an id to stamp.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth.c     |  5 +++++
 .../net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.c  | 10 +++-------
 drivers/staging/fsl_qbman/qman_high.c                  |  7 +++++--
 3 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
index edadc749c9d90..17aac2f305e36 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth.c
@@ -935,6 +935,11 @@ static int dpa_private_napi_add(struct net_device *net_dev)
 	for_each_possible_cpu(cpu) {
 		percpu_priv = per_cpu_ptr(priv->percpu_priv, cpu);
 
+		/* It drains this CPU's portal, which only this CPU's poll may
+		 * do, with DQRI masked: never from a busy-polling socket's task.
+		 * Out of the NAPI hash, as netif_napi_add_tx() keeps a NAPI, so
+		 * GRO has no id of its to stamp either. */
+		set_bit(NAPI_STATE_NO_BUSY_POLL, &percpu_priv->np.napi.state);
 		netif_napi_add(net_dev, &percpu_priv->np.napi, dpaa_eth_poll);
 	}
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.c
index 6ee57db29b176..ef3f760847177 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.c
@@ -310,13 +310,9 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(dpa_set_features);
 netdev_features_t dpa_fix_features(struct net_device *dev,
 				   netdev_features_t features)
 {
-	netdev_features_t unsupported_features = 0;
-
-	/* We don't support enabling Rx csum through ethtool yet */
-	unsupported_features |= NETIF_F_RXCSUM;
-
-	features &= ~unsupported_features;
-
+	/* Rx checksum validation is supported: dpa_set_features() switches the
+	 * parser's L4 check, and _dpa_process_parse_results() trusts it only
+	 * when the parse result says the checksum passed. */
 	return features;
 }
 
diff --git a/drivers/staging/fsl_qbman/qman_high.c b/drivers/staging/fsl_qbman/qman_high.c
index 334ca80c9ca03..4c0185bab01eb 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/fsl_qbman/qman_high.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/fsl_qbman/qman_high.c
@@ -581,8 +581,6 @@ struct dev_pm_domain qman_portal_device_pm_domain = {
 	}
 };
 
-
-
 #ifdef CONFIG_FSL_ASK_QMAN_PORTAL_NAPI
 static int qman_portal_dqrr_poll(struct napi_struct *napi, int budget)
 {
@@ -769,6 +767,11 @@ struct qman_portal *qman_create_portal(
 		pr_err("qman_portal - can't allocate the NAPI device\n");
 		goto fail_napi;
 	}
+	/* The portal is this CPU's and is drained only with DQRI masked, so its
+	 * poll must never run from a busy-polling socket's task: keep it out of
+	 * the NAPI hash, as netif_napi_add_tx() does, which also leaves GRO no
+	 * id to stamp on what it receives. */
+	set_bit(NAPI_STATE_NO_BUSY_POLL, &portal->napi.state);
 	netif_napi_add(portal->dummy_dev, &portal->napi, qman_portal_dqrr_poll);
 	napi_enable(&portal->napi);
 #endif
-- 
2.47.3

